`,s.jsxs(e.li,{children:["Before turning any knob, name what you're fixing: ",s.jsx(e.strong,{children:"bias, variance, or compute"}),". Underfit → add complexity. Overfit → add regularisation."]}),`
`,s.jsxs(e.li,{children:[s.jsx(e.strong,{children:"RF"}),": grow deep trees and let averaging handle variance. ",s.jsx(e.code,{children:"max_features"})," is the highest-leverage knob because feature subsampling can reduce correlation between trees."]}),`
